\newlabel{fig:gap-measures}{{6.1}{41}{In-sample and out-of-sample relative gaps between the unregularized joint and overlay optimizers, by risk measure and universe size. Each panel shows one risk measure, with the size of the investable universe on the horizontal axis and the risk reduction of the joint optimizer over the overlay optimizer on the vertical axis. Squares mark the mean across the $T = 91$ quarterly rebalancing dates, in blue for the in-sample gap $\tilde g_t^{\text {IS}}$ and in red for the out-of-sample gap $\tilde g_t^{\text {OOS}}$, and shaded areas mark the $95\%$ bootstrap confidence intervals}{figure.6.1}{}}
